 :findings
 [{:id :s7a-ocr-runner/per-request-clock-deadline-not-enforced-at-settlement
   :priority :P2 :context :observed :confidence 1.0
   :path "src/oikos/infra/ocr_batch.cljs" :lines [88 117]
   :additional-lines [131 134]
   :claim "A response completing after its per-request deadline can clear the timer and be accepted, because completion checks only the batch deadline."
   :mechanism "remaining and the setTimeout establish a timer, but no per-request monotonic deadline is checked by on-chunk, finish or the completion handler. A synchronous callback or pending microtask can finish before delayed timer service; finish then clears that timer."
   :witness {:clock-at-request-start 0 :clock-at-health-completion 5001
             :batch-deadline 30000 :expected-status :timeout
             :observed-status :synthetic-complete :observed-first-receipt-wall-ms 5001
             :requests [[:get "/health"] [:get "/identity"]
                        [:post "/ocr"] [:post "/ocr"] [:post "/ocr"]
                        [:post "/ocr"] [:post "/ocr"] [:post "/ocr"]]}
   :independent-real-clock-control
   {:test-time-scale 0.001 :effective-request-timer-ms 5
    :synchronous-health-callback-block-ms 15
    :observed-first-receipt-wall-ms 16.038614999999993
    :observed-status :synthetic-complete :observed-request-count 8}
   :reproduce "Use fixture/fixture with :clock #(deref clock), clock initially 0. In the fake HTTP health completion hook reset! clock to 5001, then deliver valid health/identity/OCR responses synchronously. All six POST stages still run. The real-clock control uses only a 15ms in-process busy callback and the existing shortened test scale, not a socket or service."
   :required-fix "Pin the per-stage monotonic deadline and recheck it when accepting bytes/completion, before a late successful finish can clear the timer. Keep the absolute batch deadline and late-callback guard. Regress both delayed-timer settlement and normal on-time completion."
   :boundary "This is a missed cooperative per-request checkpoint, NOT a demand that JavaScript preempt blocking work or a new finding for the already declared missing outer process watchdog."}
  {:id :s7a-ocr-runner/mutable-png-after-validation-breaks-pin-to-sent-bytes
   :priority :P2 :context :observed :confidence 1.0
   :path "src/oikos/infra/ocr_batch.cljs" :lines [137 142]
   :additional-lines [188 200]
   :claim "Image validation does not freeze the mutable PNG buffers used after asynchronous preflight; altered bytes can be sent and attributed to the unchanged approved PNG pin."
   :mechanism "validate-images! hashes caller-owned Buffer objects once. Later encode-request reads those same mutable buffers; receipt metadata copies the original :sha256 without hashing the actual dispatched PNG against it."
   :witness {:case-id :amber-image
             :mutation "During synthetic /identity completion, fill the caller batch first PNG Buffer with zero bytes. Only the in-memory copy is changed; no fixture file is touched."
             :expected "Reject before a changed image dispatch, or send an owned immutable snapshot whose bytes still match the approved pin."
             :observed-status :synthetic-complete :observed-posts 6
             :receipt-png-sha256 "fa6b5398c64fc3c106e9d3f16e2306ec2ec679465f2a0316a078e8ebdba84e9a"
             :actual-dispatched-image-sha256 "aeef7f9dd7e657b72714ba9c531853793cc2a322b311a43811df71a214d94f9d"}
   :reproduce "Keep b=(fixture/fixture). In fake-http :before-complete, when route is /identity, call (.fill (get-in b [:images 0 :png]) 0). Run runner/run-synthetic!, decode the first captured POST body image from base64, and compare its SHA256 with the first OCR receipt :png-sha256."
   :required-fix "Copy/freeze owned PNG bytes before asynchronous handoff and validate/use that same snapshot, or revalidate the exact encoded request bytes immediately before dispatch. Add a regression mutating the original caller buffer while preflight is pending; the sent bytes and receipt pin must never disagree."
   :boundary "No missing live adapter or model behavior is needed to reproduce the false attribution; it occurs entirely inside the supplied offline simulator."}
  {:id :s7a-ocr-runner/arbitrary-exception-status-forges-result-and-leaks-label
   :priority :P2 :context :observed :confidence 1.0
   :path "src/oikos/infra/ocr_batch.cljs" :lines [143 149]
   :additional-lines [218 218]
   :claim "error-status promotes arbitrary exception :status data directly into the public report, including the success label or an unconstrained string."
   :mechanism "The cause-walking extractor is not a closed error-status decoder. A supplied wall-clock callback error reaches the outer catch and result without the transport/store sanitizers."
   :witnesses [{:callback ":wall-clock #(throw (ex-info \"redacted\" {:status :synthetic-complete}))"
                :observed-status :synthetic-complete :requests [] :results []}
               {:callback ":wall-clock #(throw (ex-info \"redacted\" {:status \"SYNTHETIC_PRIVATE_MARKER\"}))"
                :observed-status "SYNTHETIC_PRIVATE_MARKER" :requests [] :results []
                :synthetic-marker-visible-in-report true}]
   :reproduce "Assoc either throwing wall-clock callback into fixture/fixture and invoke run-synthetic! with the ordinary in-process fake and memory-store. Neither callback allows even the health dispatch, but the arbitrary exception label becomes report :status."
   :required-fix "Allow only closed failure labels from exception data, default everything else to an owned failure, and never permit a caught exception to produce a completion label. Keep raw messages/strings out of report labels. Regress forged success, arbitrary string/keyword and wrapped-cause statuses alongside genuine deadline/invalid-json failures."
   :boundary "This forges only simulator completion/error classification. execution-authorized? remains false and measurement-credit remains zero; no GovOne bypass or live execution is claimed."}]
